    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-associate-rna-structure-interactions-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - RNA Structure & Interactions - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Postdoctoral Research Associate - RNA Structure & Interactions 524151 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 13 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Join a nationally significant RNA therapeutics initiative building one of the world's most data-rich RNA design platforms, with a clear pathway from AI-enabled discovery to clinical impact. Work alongside leading experts in RNA biology, structural biology, computational science and AI to develop next-generation mRNA therapeutics for hard-to-treat cancers. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 2 years, with the possibility of extension. Base salary: Level A, $116,866 p.a.  plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Australian Centre for RNA Therapeutics in Cancer (ACRTC) is a nationally significant RNA innovation hub dedicated to translating breakthrough RNA science into real treatments for aggressive cancers. Hosted by The University of Western Australia, the Centre unites RNA technologists, oncologists, computational biologists, AI and machine learning specialists, patient advocates and industry partners to solve some of the most challenging problems in cancer therapeutics. This position forms part of the RNA Optimisation for Biological Utility and Stability (ROBUST) program, a major five-year research initiative developing next-generation developing next-generation technologies to design mRNA with enhanced stability and therapeutic performance. The role offers a rare opportunity to engage directly with world leaders in RNA computation, RNA structure, cell biology and AI through scientific advisory networks, international collaborations and industry partnerships. With clearly defined clinical use cases embedded within the program, your discoveries will have a direct pathway from fundamental research to translational and clinical impact. About the opportunity Establish and apply advanced methodologies including CryoEM-based structural analysis, proteomics and mass spectrometry workflows to investigate therapeutic mRNA behaviour, function and intracellular processing. Access a globally unique RNA dataset and contribute to innovative research leading to high-impact publications, translational outcomes and intellectual property development. Work within a vibrant, collaborative and highly productive research team operating at the intersection of RNA biology, structural biology, nanotechnology, artificial intelligence and cancer therapeutics. About you PhD in molecular biology, chemistry, nanotechnology, structural biology or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research track record through peer-reviewed publications and experience in one or more relevant areas such as RNA biology, RNA-protein interactions, structural biology, CryoEM, proteomics, nanotechnology or nucleic acid-based systems. Demonstrated expertise in experimental design, data interpretation and the application of molecular biology or biochemical approaches to complex biological questions. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience working effectively across multidisciplinary teams and diverse stakeholders. Interest in translating research into real-world impact, including intellectual property development, commercialisation pathways or therapeutic innovation. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Postdoctoral Research Associate, RNA Structure & Interactions (524151).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Dr. Jessica Kretzmann at jessica.kretzmann@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday 13 September 2026 This position is open to international applicants. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 1cc63384 Last Name (required) 2fb54e4d Email (required) bfdcef8a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 757d338a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 49722bac Last Name (required) edb46eee Email (required) 31b11094 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 