    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-associate-school-of-human-sciences-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - School of Human Sciences - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Postdoctoral Research Associate - School of Human Sciences 524148 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 13 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Access a globally unique RNA dataset and collaborate with leaders in AI and RNA science. Help advance RNA and cancer therapeutics from research through to real-world applications. Part-time (0.8 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 24 months. Base salary range: Level A, $116,866 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Australian Centre for RNA Therapeutics in Cancer (ACRTC) is a nationally significant RNA innovation hub based in Western Australia, dedicated to translating cutting-edge RNA science into real treatments for aggressive cancers. The Centre brings together RNA technologists, oncologists, computational biologists, AI/ML engineers, patient advocates, and industry partners to design, synthesise, test, and optimise RNA-based medicines, with a focus on hard-to-treat cancers including sarcoma, glioblastoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, triple-negative breast cancer, lung cancer, and multiple myeloma. ACRTC is hosted by the UWA School of Human Sciences and funded by the Cancer Research Trust in collaboration with UWA, Therapeutics Innovation Australia, the WA Department of Health, Cancer Council of WA, Harry Perkins Institute, Telethon Kids Institute, Curtin University, and industry partners. ACRTC is now strengthened by a substantive funding program for the next 5 years, developing next-generation mRNA molecules with enhanced structural stability and extended therapeutic duration. Known as RNA Optimisation for Biological Utility and Stability (ROBUST), the program brings together four interconnected capabilities: (1) Computation, AI & RNA Multi-omics, (2) RNA Structure & Interactions, (3) Compartmentalisation & Condensates, and (4) Alternative RNA Formats. The findings from this interdisciplinary team will be integrated for application within identified clinical use cases, thus forging a clear path from fundamental research to clinical impact. The position sits concurrently within Capability 4: Alternative RNA Formats of the ROBUST program, where you will work as part of a team to understand how RNA structures and interactions influence stability, intracellular processing, and therapeutic performance of mRNA, and develop one of the most data-rich RNA design platforms in the world. It is concurrently situated within the RNA Innovation Foundry (RIF), ACRTC’s affiliated RNA production facility. RIF serves as the Western Australian node of a national network of RNA production facilities, offering researchers streamlined access to state-of-the-art technology and expertise in high-throughput production of RNA therapeutics for pre-clinical research. About the opportunity Design, manufacture and optimise alternative RNA formats, including circular RNA, self-amplifying RNA and alternatively polyA-tailed mRNA, to support therapeutic discovery and development in cancer. Conduct high-quality molecular biology and biochemical research, including experimental design, RNA production workflow optimisation, preliminary in vitro or cell-based testing, data interpretation and research reporting. Collaborate with interdisciplinary researchers, industry partners and external stakeholders to generate high-impact publications, support research translation and identify opportunities for intellectual property development. About you PhD in molecular biology, biochemistry or a related discipline, with a developing track record of peer-reviewed research outputs. Demonstrated experience in RNA biology, synthetic biology, genetic engineering, cell biology or a closely related area, with the ability to design and conduct rigorous independent research. Demonstrated expertise in experimental design, data interpretation and the application of molecular biology or biochemical approaches to complex biological questions. Experience working in collaborative, multidisciplinary research environments and contributing to research outcomes across teams, institutions or industry partnerships. Demonstrated interest in translating research into real-world impact, including intellectual property development, commercialisation pathways or therapeutic innovation. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Postdoctoral Research Associate (524148).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Professor Archa Fox at archa.fox@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Maddy Chaplin at maddy.chaplin@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 13 September 2026. This position is open to international applicants. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-associate-computational-rna-design-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Computational RNA Design - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Postdoctoral Research Associate - Computational RNA Design 524145 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 13 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Lead developer for the platform, driving sequence design, RNA folding and RNA stability, with access to proprietary data and a closed loop where designs are synthesised, tested and returned as training data. Interdisciplinary team at the interface of machine learning, RNA biology and cancer therapeutics, and direct engagement with world leaders and industry partners. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 24 months, with the possibility of extension. Base salary: Level A, $116,866 p.a. (pro rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Australian Centre for RNA Therapeutics in Cancer (ACRTC) is a nationally significant RNA innovation hub based in Western Australia, dedicated to translating cutting-edge RNA science into real treatments for aggressive cancers. The Centre brings together RNA technologists, oncologists, computational biologists, AI/ML engineers, patient advocates, and industry partners to design, synthesise, test, and optimise RNA-based medicines, with a focus on hard-to-treat cancers including sarcoma, glioblastoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, triple-negative breast cancer, lung cancer, and multiple myeloma. ACRTC is hosted by the UWA School of Human Sciences and funded by the Cancer Research Trust in collaboration with UWA, Therapeutics Innovation Australia, the WA Department of Health, Cancer Council of WA, Harry Perkins Institute, Telethon Kids Institute, Curtin University, and industry partners. ACRTC is now strengthened by a substantive funding program for the next 5 years, developing next-generation mRNA molecules with enhanced structural stability and extended therapeutic duration. Known as RNA Optimisation for Biological Utility and Stability (ROBUST), the program brings together four interconnected capabilities: (1) Computation, AI & RNA Multi-omics, (2) RNA Structure & Interactions, (3) Compartmentalisation & Condensates, and (4) Alternative RNA Formats. The findings from this interdisciplinary team will be integrated for application within identified clinical use cases, thus forging a clear path from fundamental research to clinical impact. This position sits within Capability 1: Computation, AI & RNA Multi-omics of the ROBUST program. Capability 1 will use a globally unique RNA dataset and state-of-the-art high-performance computing resources to develop one of the most data-rich RNA design platforms in the world. About the opportunity Develop and apply mathematical, computational, statistical and machine learning methods to RNA and multi-omics data, and build innovative design solutions to optimise next-generation mRNA molecules. Build, train, fine-tune and validate mathematical, statistical and machine learning models for RNA therapeutics, including differentiable-programming approaches, together with the computational pipelines that feed them. Work directly with experimental teams and collaborate with interdisciplinary researchers, international advisers and industry partners to run the design-build-test-learn cycle, publish high-impact research, and identify opportunities for research translation and intellectual property. About you PhD in a computational or quantitative discipline such as computer science, machine learning, mathematics, statistics, physics or engineering, computational biology. Strong background in modern machine learning, underpinned by solid foundations in linear algebra, probability, statistics and optimisation. Strong programming capability, particularly in Python and C-like languages, including a deep learning framework (PyTorch, JAX or equivalent), version control and reproducible software development practices. Demonstrated ability to reason from first principles about an unfamiliar scientific problem, and genuine appetite to develop depth in RNA biology. Demonstrated ability to contribute to high-quality research, evidenced by peer-reviewed publications, conference outputs, substantial open-source contributions or comparable scholarly achievements, and experience contributing to collaborative, multi-institutional research projects. Desirable: In-depth and innovative ML modelling, sequence models or differentiable programming; genomics or transcriptomics data, training models at scale on HPC or GPU infrastructure; and fluency with agentic and AI-assisted development workflows, applied with rigour. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Postdoctoral Research Associate (524145).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Dr Nikolay Shirokikh at nikolay.shirokikh@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Maddy Chaplin at maddy.chaplin@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 13 September 2026. This position is open to international applicants. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 73331fb6 Last Name (required) 9967e41c Email (required) 489b1202 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 056ae169 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Science Science Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 71587059 Last Name (required) a8155bb1 Email (required) 16348999 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
