    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/leukaemia-foundation-tony-fini-chair-in-blood-cancer-crawley-wa-australia-dafbad26-8335-49a5-9166-702a2b65eb4b": {
      "title": "Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer",
      "description": "Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer 524457 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 12 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Established in 1911, The University of Western Australia (UWA) is a member of Australia’s prestigious Group of Eight and one of the country’s most innovative and ambitious universities. Ranked among the Top 100 universities globally, UWA is committed to creating knowledge and transforming lives through leading-edge teaching, learning and research spanning a broad range of disciplines. The University is seeking an outstanding leader in Blood Cancer Research to become the inaugural Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer, based within either the School of Biomedical Science or UWA Medical School. This is a rare opportunity to shape the future of blood cancer research and drive national and global progress through world-class research, collaboration and translation. The Chair, secured through a generous, endowed donation, will have the platform to build an enduring programme of research and make a lasting contribution to the field. As Chair, you will provide intellectual and strategic leadership to an ambitious research agenda advancing the understanding, prevention, detection, diagnosis or treatment of blood cancer and related disorders. UWA welcomes candidates with deep expertise in one or more areas of significant opportunity, including prevention, early detection, diagnostics, precision medicine, discovery or translational research, across adult or paediatric blood cancers. You will bring an internationally excellent research profile, demonstrated success in securing competitive funding and a strong record of high-quality outputs, together with the influence and collaborative approach to build partnerships across academia, clinical practice, government, industry, professional bodies and philanthropy. The successful candidate will be an exceptional academic and team leader, with a recognised doctoral qualification and an outstanding record in blood cancer or related disorders research. You will have demonstrated success in building and mentoring high-performing research teams, developing emerging talent and translating complex scientific concepts for diverse audiences. You will champion the highest standards of research integrity and governance, while engaging meaningfully with consumers, communities and the broader Western Australian health and research ecosystem. Above all, you will bring the vision, credibility and ambition to establish a sustainable, internationally recognised research programme and create a legacy in blood cancer research. How to Apply The University of Western Australia has partnered with Perrett Laver on this appointment. For a conversation in confidence please contact: Tadhg Waddington ( Tadhg.waddington@perrettlaver.com ). For further information and to apply, please submit a CV and covering letter on the Perrett Laver website , detailing how you fulfill the role description and personal specification, quoting reference 8619 . The deadline for applications is Monday, 12 October at 9:00am AWST . If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise us of these so that we can make appropriate arrangements. Perrett Laver’s Privacy Statement Perrett Laver Pty Ltd collects and uses personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles. Your data is held securely and used only for the purpose for which it was provided. For our full Privacy Statement, visit https://perrettlaver.com/privacy-policy/ If you have comments that would support us to improve access to documentation, or our application processes more generally, please do not hesitate to contact us via accessibility@perrettlaver.com . UWA commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 5568cb6d Last Name (required) 6d615341 Email (required) 5724c4f6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Senior Software Developer Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a multidisciplinary team advancing photonic systems for astronomy and space science. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9611a2b2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 469677b2 Last Name (required) 1103eb95 Email (required) 612c4c84 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
