    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/category-manager-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Category Manager",
      "description": "Category Manager - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Category Manager 524295 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 28 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Lead strategic procurement and category management at one of Australia's leading research-intensive universities. Develop and deliver against category strategies that achieve value for money, mitigate supply and commercial risks, and support sustainable procurement outcomes across the University. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: Level 9, $139,660 – $147,783 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area Finance supports the University through the delivery of strategic financial advice, governance, procurement, financial performance, compliance, and operational services. The Procurement team partners with stakeholders across the University to deliver value-driven sourcing solutions, optimise expenditure, strengthen supplier relationships, and support the University's strategic objectives. As part of this function, the Procurement team works with academic and professional areas across the University to ensure best-practice procurement, commercial risk management, sustainable sourcing, and effective contract management. About the opportunity Lead the development and execution of category management strategies, strategic sourcing initiatives, and procurement plans that maximise value, support sustainability objectives, and strengthen supply chain resilience. Provide expert commercial advice on procurement, contract negotiation, supplier performance, risk management, contract and supplier management and value optimisation while partnering with stakeholders across the University. Lead and develop a high-performing procurement team, driving continuous improvement, capability uplift, compliance, and best-practice procurement outcomes. About you Relevant postgraduate qualification, MCIPS accreditation, or equivalent demonstrated procurement and commercial expertise. Extensive experience in category management, strategic sourcing, contract management, supplier relationship management, and procurement across diverse spend categories. Proven leadership experience with the ability to manage teams, resources, projects, and organisational priorities in a complex environment. Strong commercial and analytical capability, with demonstrated success negotiating complex commercial agreements and delivering measurable value outcomes. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication, presentation, and influencing skills, with the ability to provide trusted advice and procurement training to diverse audiences. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Category Manager - 524295.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Emma Gillespie at emma.gillespie@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 28 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 5783648a Last Name (required) 8204d996 Email (required) ee4f77ff Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Senior Software Developer Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a multidisciplinary team advancing photonic systems for astronomy and space science. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b02269a6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Finance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA,