    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-software-developer-crawley-wa-australia-c8cfb51c-4432-4773-a318-38677e3dedda": {
      "title": "Senior Software Developer",
      "description": "Senior Software Developer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Software Developer 524449 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 4 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Senior Software Developer (521717) Play a key role in the development of software for the Square Kilometre Array (SKA), the world’s largest radio telescope. Join a multidisciplinary team advancing photonic systems for astronomy and space science. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 2 years. Base salary range: $108,413– $120,287 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR) is a joint venture between Curtin University and The University of Western Australia (UWA), established in 2009 and funded through 2030 with $65 million from the WA State Government. ICRAR is a leading institution in radio astronomy and a key Australian contributor to the global SKA project. The Astrophotonics Group within ICRAR develops advanced photonic systems for radio and optical astronomy, with a focus on long-distance transfer of stabilised frequency and timing signals via optical fibre and free-space laser links. About the opportunity Lead software development for the Phase Synchronisation System (PSS) of the SKA-Mid telescope. Collaborate with engineers, scientists, and external partners to deliver robust, scalable software solutions. Contribute to both office-based development and laboratory-based testing and integration. About you Tertiary qualification in computer science, software engineering, electrical engineering, or a related field, with demonstrated software development experience. Proficient in C++, Python, MySQL, TCL, SCPI commands, and Assembly. Experienced in AGILE development, version control (Git), and collaborative workflows. Skilled in software documentation and deployment practices. Strong problem-solving and organisational skills, with the ability to work independently. Applicants with an electrical engineering background and strong software development experience are encouraged to apply. Position description: Senior Software Developer PD.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact zander.ribbens@uwa.edu.au. How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on 04 October 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 2ed421e5 Last Name (required) 3b4d78c2 Email (required) c6ce55e9 Refe