    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/administrative-officer-podiatry-casual-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Administrative Officer, Podiatry",
      "description": "Administrative Officer, Podiatry  - (Casual) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Administrative Officer, Podiatry  - (Casual) 524355 Crawley, WA Casual Closing on: 27 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Play an important role in delivering exceptional front-of-house customer service and patient support within a busy clinic environment. Join a supportive and professional team where you will help create a positive experience for patients, students, clinicians and visitors. Casual appointment. About the opportunity Manage patient bookings, appointment scheduling and reception services, ensuring a welcoming and efficient experience for all clinic visitors. Maintain accurate patient records and clinic documentation, process payments, respond to enquiries and support day-to-day clinic operations. Liaise effectively with patients, students, clinicians and external stakeholders while providing administrative support for teaching and clinical activities. About you Demonstrated administrative, reception or customer service experience, ideally within a healthcare, medical practice, allied health or clinic environment. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, work independently and use sound judgment in a fast-paced setting. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with a commitment to delivering exceptional customer service and patient care. Proven ability to work collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team while building positive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, email systems, databases and administrative software. Current National Police Clearance Certificate and current Working with Children Check. Flexibility to work a variety of shifts as required. Desirable Skills Experience using medical practice software (such as Genie or similar systems) alongside experience within a healthcare, clinic setting and coordinating appointment schedules will be highly regarded. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday 27 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Application Details: Please email Nicola Deabreu at nicola.deabreu@uwa.edu.au with the following Current CV/resume Copy of relevant qualifications A brief cover letter outlining your suitability for the role and relevant administrative experience Shortlisted applicants will be contacted for further discussion. If you have any questions regarding the positions and UWA, please contact ­­­­­­­­­the Clinic Coordinator: Nicola Deabreu nicola.deabreu@uwa.edu.au Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 00c569a6 Last Name (required) 8a080122 Email (required) c62396b6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e471fd86 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration & Executive support Administration & Executive support Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) b7369d3a Last Name (required) bf05d9c2 Email (required) 3607abf1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you