    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-marketing-officer-priority-programs-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Marketing Officer, Priority Programs",
      "description": "Senior Marketing Officer, Priority Programs - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Marketing Officer, Priority Programs 524346 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 27 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Deliver audience-led, high-quality marketing and communications initiatives that drive student growth, access, participation and success for equity and priority cohorts. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 18 months. Base salary range: $108,413 – $120,287 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Brand, Marketing and Recruitment (BMR) division brings together marketing, communications, engagement and events to strengthen UWA’s reputation and support student growth. Within BMR, the Marketing Performance and Operations team drives student acquisition through integrated marketing, digital experience, CRM, marketing automation, lead nurture and performance optimisation. Working across domestic and international recruitment, the team delivers audience-led campaigns and strategies that connect prospective students with opportunities at UWA. This role sits within the Schools Marketing and Priority Programs portfolio and supports major University initiatives designed to improve access, participation and success for students from equity and priority cohorts, including Indigenous students, regional and remote communities, and students from low socio-economic backgrounds. About the opportunity Lead the delivery of integrated, multi-channel marketing campaigns and communications that support student recruitment, engagement and participation among Indigenous students and those from regional, remote and low socio-economic communities, fostering greater diversity, accessibility and inclusion. Develop audience-led content, campaigns and storytelling that promote scholarships, pathways and educational opportunities across the prospective student journey, driving awareness, consideration and conversion. Build and sustain strong stakeholder relationships, developing a deep understanding of business priorities, audience needs and barriers to engagement to coordinate integrated marketing initiatives that improve access, participation and outcomes for priority cohorts. About you Relevant tertiary qualification, or equivalent demonstrated experience. Substantial experience delivering integrated marketing and communications initiatives, including end-to-end campaign development and execution across a wide range of channels and touchpoints, with a strong commitment to brand governance and consistency. Highly developed stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build and sustain effective relationships across internal and external stakeholders, demonstrate strong business acumen, and coordinate cross-team input to achieve outcomes Demonstrated experience in lifecycle marketing strategy and multi-channel implementation, with sound knowledge of go-to-market planning, audience segmentation, proposition development and content planning. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Occasional travel within Western Australia may be required, along with occasional after-hours or weekend work. There may also be a requirement to work during parts of the Christmas/New Year period. Position description: PD - Senior Marketing Officer, Priority Programs (524346).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Emily McCarthy at emily.mccarthy@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 27 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) dfe7296c Last Name (required) 1ca58ee4 Email (required) bf2f8e1e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 1c567598 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community Engagement/Marketing Community Engagement/Marketing Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 7188292a Last Name (required) 419e81b3 Email (required) e04aa101 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/casual-project-administrative-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Casual",
      "description": "Casual - Project Administrative Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Casual - Project Administrative Officer 524403 Crawley, WA Casual Closing on: 20 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Casual, part-time (0.6 FTE, negotiable) appointment. About the opportunity Provide high-quality administrative and project support for the Einstein-First Project, a nationally significant curriculum reform initiative based within the School of Physics, Mathematics and Computing at UWA, supporting the delivery of research, education and outreach activities. Coordinate meetings, calendars, communications and stakeholder engagement activities, including liaison with participating schools, researchers, government representatives, donors and other external partners. Support project operations through records management, research data administration, ethics documentation, website content coordination, newsletters, event administration and maintenance of shared digital resources and contact databases. Assist with the planning, promotion and delivery of teacher professional learning programs, seminars, outreach activities and other events that contribute to improving STEM engagement and education outcomes. About you Relevant administrative qualifications and demonstrated experience in administration, project coordination, office management or a similar support role. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with strong attention to detail and the ability to prepare, edit and maintain accurate, professional documentation. Strong organisational and time management skills, with a proven ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate multiple activities simultaneously and consistently meet deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work independently, show initiative, solve problems and collaborate effectively within a small, high-performing team. Proficiency across Microsoft Office applications, databases, online collaboration tools, email systems and digital platforms, together with experience maintaining records and stakeholder information. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 20 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Application Details: Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fbe1e663 Last Name (required) 1c0d7d44 Email (required) 439b8857 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 383fa3ef Finalize your job alert by selecting