    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/solution-architect-crawley-wa-australia-06b8ec6c-338c-4b92-a693-c347a5d67444": {
      "title": "Solution Architect",
      "description": "Solution Architect - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Solution Architect 524205 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 17 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Shape infrastructure solutions that underpin teaching, research and enterprise services. Provide hands-on technical solution architecture across hybrid cloud, networks, compute, storage and platform services. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $139,660 – $147,783 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area UWA is making significant investments in Information and Technology Services to enable its strategic direction and goals. The Platforms and Operations portfolio provides the foundational infrastructure, platforms and operational capabilities that support the University’s teaching, research and professional services environments. Robust, secure and well-governed infrastructure architecture is vital to ensuring that cloud, data centre, network, endpoint, integration and classroom technology services are reliable, scalable and aligned to enterprise architecture and operational standards. About the opportunity Work specifically across the IT infrastructure domain, developing and guiding multidisciplinary solution architectures for hybrid cloud, data centre, network, storage, endpoint and related platform services. Translate project, business and technology requirements into practical infrastructure designs, patterns and implementation guidance that align with long-term strategy, roadmaps and enterprise architecture direction. Provide senior technical leadership for platform transitions, technology upgrades and infrastructure lifecycle management, including design reviews, risk assessment, implementation planning and transition to support. About you You bring either a postgraduate qualification, extensive senior-level experience, or a strong combination of relevant education, training and practical experience. You have credible technical depth in cloud, infrastructure, networking, security or solution architecture, supported by relevant certifications or equivalent demonstrated experience. You are comfortable working across complex infrastructure environments, such as Azure, data centres, compute, storage, virtualisation, networks, endpoint platforms, automation, monitoring or related security controls. You can lead technical design conversations, test assumptions, document clear recommendations and bring project, architecture, cyber security and operations stakeholders with you. You bring a positive, can-do mindset, enjoy working with autonomy, and are able to balance strategic intent with practical delivery constraints while building trusted relationships with technical and non-technical colleagues. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Solution Architect 524205.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Jamie Graham at jamie.graham@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 17 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 83b9b282 Last Name (required) b92ad717 Email (required) 316c214e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9066dc50 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 909f383f Last Name (required) 5ba3e192 Email (required) 7bd191ab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
