    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-cybersecurity-architecture-specialist-crawley-wa-australia-df19d5e6-8e7a-472c-81fc-65e7107534b2": {
      "title": "Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist",
      "description": "Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist 524328 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites An exciting opportunity to champion secure-by-design and DevSecOps practices across the University. Collaborative team culture and flexible work arrangements that support work-life balance. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $139,660 – $147,783 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area UWA is making significant investments in the Information and Technology Services area to enable its strategic direction and goals. Cybersecurity is one of these areas and is undergoing an uplift in capability and delivery of new services to align with the University’s risk strategy. The Cybersecurity & Technology Risk unit provides risk governance, architecture & design assurance, and operational governance to all aspects of the cyber security domain, from network security, platform security, application development, cyber awareness and education, and security operations. About the opportunity As a senior member of the Cybersecurity & Technology Risk team, you will provide expert cyber security advisory and assurance services across a diverse portfolio of technology initiatives. You will work closely with project teams, solution owners, developers and operational stakeholders to assess cyber risks, evaluate security controls and embed secure-by-design principles into solutions from concept through to deployment. Operating as a trusted advisor, you will help shape secure outcomes across cloud, infrastructure, applications and modern deployment pipelines while ensuring initiatives align with UWA's cyber security framework and risk management objectives. You will also lead security assessments, assurance activities and governance initiatives that strengthen the University's overall cyber resilience. About you Relevant post graduate qualification or demonstrated equivalent competency. Demonstrated experience conducting security assessments, assurance reviews, control validation activities or secure-by-design reviews across cloud, infrastructure, application and DevSecOps environments is highly desirable Extensive experience providing cyber security advisory, assurance or consulting services across complex technology environments, including cloud, applications, infrastructure and modern deployment pipelines. Strong knowledge of cyber security frameworks (ISO 27001, NIST, ASD ISM) and the ability to apply these frameworks pragmatically to support risk-based decision making and secure outcomes. Relevant industry certifications, including SABSA Foundations, TOGAF, CEH, CISSP, CISM or other security/control certifications are desirable Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist 524328.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Goran Mitrovic at goran.mitrovic@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 20 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a70024f9 Last Name (required) 40ca16ce Email (required) 2c2eef7e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8f5d1be7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) abf2e6c5 Last Name (required) 0d8260f7 Email (required) c0f8dd8d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/school-operations-officer-music-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "School Operations Officer (Music)",
      "description": "School Operations Officer (Music) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel School Operations Officer (Music) 524306 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 17 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Join a vibrant environment at one of Australia’s leading University Music Schools. Support student, academic & performance operations across the UWA Conservatorium of Music. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $86,540 – $95,920 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area College Services provides academic administration and operational support to the University’s schools, helping deliver exceptional outcomes for students, researchers and academic staff. Within this environment, the UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement across classical music, contemporary popular music, electronic music and sound design, and music theatre. The Conservatorium delivers an extensive program of concerts, productions, outreach initiatives and teaching activities, working closely with students, staff, visiting artists, industry partners and the broader community. About the opportunity Coordinate a broad range of school operations activities, including student and HDR administration, scholarships and prizes, committee support, website updates, timetabling, room scheduling and day-to-day office operations. Support prospective student engagement and the audition process through candidate communications, audition scheduling and liaison with key university stakeholders. Collaborate across College Operations and University teams to deliver high-quality administrative services, provide stakeholder support, drive continuous improvement initiatives and contribute to the success of Conservatorium teaching, research and engagement activities. About you Relevant tertiary qualification or an equivalent combination of education, training and substantial administrative experience. Demonstrated experience providing high-quality administrative support in a complex organisation, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships and provide outstanding customer service to diverse stakeholders. Strong organisational, problem-solving and coordination skills, with the ability to work independently, exercise initiative and contribute as part of a collaborative team. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and administrative systems, including experience working with databases, spreadsheets, email and online platforms. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current WA Working with Children Check will be required by the successful applicant. Some after-hours work is required to support concert, performance and outreach activities. Position description: PD - School Operations Officer (Music) (524306).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Sarah Brittenden at sarah.brittenden@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 17 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b296f3b1 Last Name (required) 6d3814c5 Email (required) 656fac58 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Leukaemia Foundation Tony Fini Chair in Blood Cancer Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Lead transformational blood cancer research with national reach and international influence, supported by a landmark partnership with the Leukaemia Foundation Associate Lecturer Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career in a highly ranked department with opportunities to contribute to both impactful research and university teaching. Category Manager Crawley, WA Finance Maternity leave cover | Flexible working arrangements | Lead strategic procurement across a high-performing procurement team Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 7be4b667 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Administration / Support Services Student Administration / Support Services Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) ceb4e2c3 Last Name (required) 133197e1 Email (required) 95550f28 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the ope